# Mass Assignment Reviewer Rule v1.0 STRICT

**Do not inline-audit.** Invoke **`mass_assignment_reviewer`** -> `.cursor/agents/mass_assignment_reviewer.md`.

## References

| Artifact | Path |
|---|---|
| Policy | `.cursor/skills/mass_assignment_reviewer/POLICY.md` |
| Scan skill | `.cursor/skills/mass_assignment_reviewer/SKILL.md` |
| Report path | `AI/mass_assignment_reviewer/mass_assignment_reviewer_report.md` |
| Report line | `mass_assignment_reviewer v1.0 STRICT` |

**POLICY.md wins.**

## Invoke when

Use before deploy or when controller endpoints, `@RequestBody` / `@ModelAttribute` payload DTOs, object mapping logic (`BeanUtils`, MapStruct), Jackson configurations, or sensitive business logic derivation change.

Skip for generated output, `target/`, `node_modules/`, and docs-only edits unless the docs define data binding policy.

## Non-negotiable rules

1. **Binding external inputs directly into JPA `@Entity` classes is always FAIL.**
2. **Allowing clients to submit `role`, `isAdmin`, `price`, or `ownerId` in request payloads is always FAIL.**
3. **Using broad object mappers (e.g., `BeanUtils.copyProperties`) directly onto entities without an explicit allow-list is always FAIL.**

